fxe5 22. Rf2 Bd7 23. Ref1 Rd8 24. Qe2 Nh8 25. Bd2 Bc8 26. Qe3 a6 27. b4 Rd7 28.
Bc4 Qg6 29. g4 Rf7 30. a3 Rgf8 31. Bc1 Qf6 32. Kg1 b5 33. Bd5 Qd8 34. h4 Rg8
35. Rh2 Rg6 36. hxg5 Nxg5 37. Bxf7 Nhxf7 38. Rh5 d5 39. dxe5 dxe4 40. Kh1 Nxe5
41. Nxh6 Rxh6 {(sealed move)} 42. Qxg5 Qxg5 43. Bxg5 Rxh5+ 44. gxh5 Be6 45. Bf4
Ng4 46. Kg2 c6 47. Kg3 Nf6 48. Kh4 Nd5 49. Be5 e3 50. Rf8 {BCM 1923, p321,
gives the moves to here only...} Bg8 51. Ra8 e2 52. Ra7+ Kh6 53. Bg7+ Kh7 54.
Bf6+ Bf7 55. Rxf7+ Kg8 56. Rg7+ Kf8 57. Rg1 Nxf6 58. Re1 {"and wins" (The
Observer, 26 Aug 1923)} Nd5 59. Rxe2 Nxc3 60. Rc2 {Sources: Tinsley notebooks;
The Times, 27 Aug 1923; Manchester Guardian, 27 Aug 1923; Glasgow Herald, 1
Sept 1923; (41w-50w) BCM, September 1923, p321. Gibson, having lost his first
round game in 20 minutes, took five hours to win his last game (and thereby
deprived Yates of the Championship) (Falkirk Herald, 5 September 1923)} 1-0

