interesting possibility was:} 27. Nxg6 $1 Nxg3 $1 28. Qf6 $1 Rh1+ 29. Kg2 Rh2+
30. Kg1 Kh7 31. Ne5 Rh1+ 32. Kg2 Rxe1 33. Rxe1 Re6 34. Qxf7+ Qxf7 35. Nxf7 Ne4
{(Alekhine)" (BCM, September, p324)}) 27... Qd6 28. Qf3 Rh5 29. Nf4 Rf5 30. Re2
Qd7 31. Qh1 ({"White should have played} 31. Qg2 {instead of 31.Qh1" (BCM,
September, p324)}) 31... Kh7 32. Rec2 g5 33. Nd3 Nxg3 34. fxg3 Rxe3 35. Nf2
Rxg3+ 36. Kf1 Qxd4 37. Re2 Rgf3 38. Rcc2 Qd1+ 39. Kg2 Qd5 40. Kg1 Rg3+ 41. Kh2
Rxf2+ 42. Rxf2 Rh3+ 43. Kxh3 Qxh1+ {Sources: Yorkshire Post and Leeds
Intelligencer, 20 August 1923; The Observer, 19 Aug 1923; Glasgow Herald, 22
Sept 1923; BCM, September 1923, p323} ({Modern databases such as StarBase 4.56
and Mega 2016 quote the finish as} 43... Qxh1+ 44. Kg4 Qe4+ 45. Kg3 f5) 0-1

