"MissScarlett" has commented: Skinner & Verhoeven: <Only the first ten moves
of the following game are available. An account of the game appeared in the
<Birmingham Post>, 18 August 1923, p.12: "Alekhine caught Groen in the opening.
He defended with 5...Bc5, the Classical Defence and picked up a pawn very
early. Later the Dutch player allowed ...Bh3, the bishop not being able to be
taken on account of ...Nf3+ winning the queen. Groen resigned on the 23rd move
without waiting to be mated.">} 0-1

