1. d4 Nf6 (1... d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Be7 5. e3 Nbd7 6. Nf3 O-O {
is the sequence of opening moves given in BCM but not by Alekhine himself in
his best game collection}) 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 d5 4. Nc3 Be7 5. Bg5 Nbd7 6. e3 O-O
7. Rc1 c6 8. Bd3 Re8 9. O-O dxc4 10. Bxc4 Nd5 11. Ne4 Bxg5 12. Nfxg5 N7f6 13.
Ng3 h6 14. Nf3 Nb6 15. Bb3 Nbd7 16. e4 e5 17. dxe5 Ng4 18. e6 fxe6 19. Nd4 Nde5
{(BCM gives this as '19... KKt-K4' so it should be the d-knight which comes to
e5 as it started its life on g8)} 20. h3 Nf6 21. f4 Nf7 22. Kh1 a5 23. Rc3 Qb6
24. e5 Nd5 25. Nh5 Re7 26. Rg3 Nh8 27. Qd3 Qc7 28. Bxd5 exd5 29. Nf6+ {Sources:
My Best Games of Chess 1908-23 by Alexander Alekhine; BCM, November 1923, p423}
({Extra moves appended:} 29. Nf6+ Kf8 30. Qh7 {Source: StarBase 4.56}) 1-0

