1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. Nxe5 d6 4. Nf3 Nxe4 5. d4 d5 6. Bd3 Be7 7. O-O Bg4 8. c4
f5 9. Qa4+ c6 10. Ne5 Bh5 11. Nc3 O-O 12. cxd5 Nxc3 13. bxc3 cxd5 14. c4 Kh8
15. Qb3 Nc6 16. Nxc6 bxc6 17. cxd5 cxd5 18. Rb1 f4 19. Ba3 f3 20. Bxe7 Qxe7 21.
Qxd5 fxg2 22. Rfe1 Qf6 23. Rb2 Bf3 24. Qe5 Qh4 25. Reb1 Rae8 26. Rb8 Bb7 {
Sources: Yorkshire Post and Leeds Intelligencer, 20 August 1923; Glasgow
Herald, 8 Sept 1923; (final position) BCM, September 1923, p328} (26... Bb7 {
Here F.C. Short pointed out} 27. Qf5 $5 {but} Rxb8 (27... Bc8 $1 $19 {was
pointed out by RW Barnett in a letter to BCM, November 1923, p413: "... it is
suggested that the resignation was premature and that White had 'a brilliant
resource' in 27.Qf5. I admit the brilliancy of this move but not its soundness,
for 27...Bc8 wins out of hand. Such, however, is the intricacy and beauty of
the position that the numerous analysts who examined it after White's
resignation seem all to have overlooked this cogent reply!"}) 28. Rxb7 Rbe8 29.
Re7 Rd8 30. Rf7 Rxf7 31. Qxf7 Qxd4 $19 {wins}) 0-1

